<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhine Crisis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1840">1840</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Rhine Crisis of 1840</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> Crisis of 1840 was a diplomatic confrontation in which the French government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolphe-thiers">Adolphe Thiers</a>, humiliated in the Eastern Question, raised demands for the Rhine as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s eastern frontier. The threat provoked a wave of German national feeling, expressed in patriotic songs such as Die Wacht am Rhein, and led the German Confederation to strengthen its federal fortresses, including new ones at Ulm and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rastatt">Rastatt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhine-crisis.jpg" alt="Rhine Crisis" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was kgberger at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deutscher_Bund_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
